cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Sulu Mangrove Dynamics GeoAI: reproducibility code and derived results"
message: "If you use this software or its derived results, please cite the Zenodo release DOI and the associated article when available."
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Remagorp2016/sulu-mangrove-dynamics-geoai"
authors:
  - family-names: "Adju"
    given-names: "Fadzlur-Nijar A."
    affiliation: "Mindanao State University-Sulu"
    email: "fadzlur-nijar.adju@msusulu.edu.ph"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-1865-7596"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility code and lightweight derived results for an uncertainty-aware analysis
  of three decades of mangrove persistence, turnover, and expansion in Sulu Province,
  Philippines. The workflow harmonizes Continuous Global Mangrove Dynamics and Global
  Mangrove Watch v4.1.12, quantifies cross-product uncertainty, identifies consensus
  spatial hotspots, and evaluates interpretable machine-learning models with spatially
  blocked validation for environmental-management screening.
keywords:
  - mangrove dynamics
  - Global Mangrove Watch
  - Continuous Global Mangrove Dynamics
  - GeoAI
  - explainable machine learning
  - SHAP
  - spatial cross-validation
  - environmental management
  - Sulu
  - Philippines
